<p>Rebrand year — Make Football Great Again, and keepers arrived to make the
drafts worse. David won the regular season and the biggest check, then
face-planted in the playoffs. Jeremy took the ring from the two-seed and let
David keep the receipt.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Fraud</h3>
<p>David went 11-4, luckier than anyone had a right to be. He collected
<span class="stat">$950</span> for the regular season and then finished 4th in the
actual playoffs, which is the David special. Justin was right behind him, 10-5 and
lucky as hell.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Robbed</h3>
<p>Cory scored <span class="stat">1830.64</span>, second-most in the entire
league, and missed the playoffs. He lost the last seed to Marian on the season
points tiebreaker by <span class="stat">8.20</span>. Over fifteen weeks. With a team
named "Zero Mistakes Were Made."</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Weird</h3>
<p>Michael's Josh Allen went for <span class="stat">57.88</span> in Week 14, the
best single game anyone had all year, and Michael still went 6-9 and missed the
playoffs. Sam finished with the lowest points scored and the most points allowed,
a full <span class="stat">1857</span> against, which takes real commitment. Cory
beat him by 75 in Week 5 just to twist it.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Margins</h3>
<p>Jeremy missed the Week 1 high by <span class="stat">0.12</span>. Cory missed
the Week 15 high by 1.06. And in a Week 15 loss, Jeremy benched Jared Goff for
51.06 — then went and won the whole thing anyway.</p>

<div class="respect"><p class="crown">The Champion</p><p>Jeremy rode the two-seed
to the ring for <span class="stat">$900</span> — and did it the week after benching
Jared Goff for 51.06 in a loss, because the football gods have a sense of humor.</p></div>

<p>David got the most money and no ring. Cory scored the second-most points in
the league and got four hundred bucks and a tiebreaker to think about all
offseason.</p>
